From: Josh Vanderberg <jvanderberg@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tcc native armv7m: no MemAvailable reserve check (ATRANS pool and swap)

On native Arm Linux tcc runs as an ATRANS program; its memory comes from
the ATRANS pool and swap, which MemAvailable does not count, so the
512 kB reserve check stops compiles that fit (stackfall with tmux, mc
and four logins up). A real shortage still shows as a failed allocation:
the page-cache drop and retry, then "memory full".
---
--- a/libtcc.c
+++ b/libtcc.c
@@ -263,6 +263,14 @@
     long kb;
     int fd, n;
 
+#ifdef TCC_ARM_THUMB
+    /* Native Arm Linux: tcc is an ATRANS program, and its memory comes
+       from the ATRANS pool and swap, which MemAvailable doesn't count, so
+       this check stopped compiles that fit. A real shortage shows as a
+       failed allocation instead (mem_drop_caches, then "memory full"). */
+    (void)size;
+    return;
+#endif
     since_check += size;
     if (since_check < MEM_CHECK_STEP)
         return;
